<poml>
    <task>
        Interrogate a Gantry Bench evidence bundle: report what the verdict concluded and
        what the underlying tables actually support, using auditable SQL for every number.
        <stepwise-instructions>
            <list listStyle="decimal">
                <item>
                    Call describe_data_source on the bundle path. Create a "Verdict" section
                    quoting each gate's one-line summary from the source metadata, in gate
                    order (g0 intake, g1 data report, g2 signal check, g3 robot test).
                </item>
                <item>
                    Create a "Signal check, clip by clip" section. Query the signal_pairs
                    topic: count clips where the real pairing beat its shuffled control
                    (better = true), and list the three thinnest margins
                    (error_shuffled - error_yours, ascending) with their episode ids. A thin
                    margin is a clip whose visual-action correspondence barely survived the
                    control; name them so the owner can watch exactly those clips.
                </item>
                <item>
                    Create a "Where the ladder breaks" section. Query the ladder topic:
                    success rate per rung per arm, ordered by rung_index. Identify the first
                    rung where the rate drops sharply. Treat NULL rates as "not measured" and
                    say so; never present an unmeasured rung as a zero.
                </item>
                <item>
                    Create a "What to fix" section. Query the findings topic for rows with
                    severity above info, and join each against the coach topic's fix rows on
                    the finding code, so every problem appears beside the recorded advice for
                    it. If the coach table is absent, present the findings alone and say the
                    bundle carries no coaching.
                </item>
                <item>
                    End with an "Honesty notes" section: whether a shuffled control arm was
                    present in the robot test (g3_context.has_control in the source
                    metadata), any abstained modules with their reasons, and any rung the
                    baseline never measured. These are the caveats the bench itself attaches;
                    do not soften them.
                </item>
            </list>
        </stepwise-instructions>
        Every number in the report must come from a SQL query over the bundle's topics or
        verbatim from the source metadata. If a question cannot be answered from the tables
        present, say so plainly rather than estimating; a bundle is allowed to be missing a
        gate, and the honest answer there is "not run", not a guess.
    </task>

    <output-format>
        A markdown report with the five sections above. Keep each SQL query you ran visible
        in a code block beside the numbers it produced, so the owner can audit every claim.
    </output-format>
</poml>
